{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrztvyJRWW2afB23q1qA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`export/core.py` now dispatches through a registry, and the three formats live in `export/formats/`. The 5 existing tests pass. I also checked that `export.names()` returns `['csv', 'json', 'xml']`. An unknown format gives `unknown format 'yaml'; known formats: csv, json, xml`.\n\n- **Base class:** `export/base.py` has `Exporter` with `name`, `extension` and `dump(records) -> bytes`.\n- **Registry:** `export/registry.py` has `register` (usable as a class decorator), `get`, `names` and `UnknownFormat`. `register` raises if a class is not an `Exporter` subclass or lacks a `name` or `extension`.\n- **Formats:** `export/formats/csv.py`, `json.py` and `xml.py` each register one exporter. `formats/__init__.py` imports every module in the package automatically, and `export/__init__.py` imports `formats`, so they are registered on `import export`.\n- **`core.py`:** `export_records` and `export_to_file` keep their signatures and behaviour, with no per-format code left. A new format needs only a new module in `export/formats/` that uses `@register`.\n- **Exports:** `import export` now also exposes `Exporter`, `register`, `get` and `names`.\n\nI made no commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4927,"cache_read_input_tokens":27622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4927},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f01aae0a-5db9-4f6e-8dcf-f5cf4a87e8ed","uuid":"8179d01d-bb04-4736-965b-fc1d1f931bb8","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:43:49.438Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrztvbyta5yk34UPveHt"}
